WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.101
We're staying on top of

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.535
breaking news out of South Korea.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.436
Officials now say

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.239
at least 59 people have been killed

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.241
and some 150 others

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.076
injured during a Halloween event.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.011
In Seoul.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.379
CNN's Will Ripley

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:13.947
is there now on the scene.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:16.149
Well, what are you learning

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.285
Fred, arriving here.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.121
We got this stunning news

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.655
from from the fire

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.623
officials who have been

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.025
responding out here.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.494
About 900 or so police and firefighters

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:28.628
here on the scene.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.997
And the news is just about as bad as

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.767
as we could have imagined.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.568
I was walking past people

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.771
in Halloween costumes on the phone,

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:40.040
absolutely sobbing,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.307
calling their family members

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.176
to let them know that they're okay.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.177
You can see that

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.346
there are stretchers out here

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.013
waiting to see

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.148
if there are any more people

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.516
who need to be taken to the hospital.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:53.019
But the videos that have been appearing

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.254
on social media, combined

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.488
with the emergency alerts,

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.823
we knew that something

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.892
something really awful had happened here.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.860
This is to set the scene for you, Fred.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.162
This is the Itaewon.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.830
Is it possible to go through here, CNN,

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.631
just through here. Thank you.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.434
This is the Itaewon

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.902
nightclub district in Seoul.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.137
It is iconic for

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.707
among other major holidays, Halloween.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:15.809
People fly in

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.178
from all over the region here in Asia

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:19.312
to come here

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.814
to celebrate Halloween in Itaewon.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:21.681
Come over here, Charlie.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.450
If we can just let's see.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.617
I just want to take you down

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:27.954
this row of emergency vehicles here.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.557
And you can see this line of stretchers.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.926
So so all the hotels

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.993
in this area are sold out.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.229
And it was actually at the Hamilton Hotel

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.864
which is right here to my right.

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.966
To my left. Excuse me.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.668
There was a

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:42.435
Halloween party,

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.370
and apparently some sort of an incident

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.506
happened. People fell down.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.775
It's been described in local media

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.310
as a stampede,

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.744
but people essentially were crushed.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:52.412
They fell.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.381
Let's get a closer here.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.417
And people raced out into the street.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.051
A lot of the streets

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.519
here are very, very densely packed.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:00.019
There were

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.589
tens of thousands of people out here.

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.091
And the videos on social media showed

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.993
people in costume

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.896
lying on the ground, not moving

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.865
and suffered cardiac arrest.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.233
We now know.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:16.136
59 of those people at least

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:17.370
did not make it.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.240
And so the videos that we that we saw

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.941
and we were afraid that people

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.209
might might actually be dead

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:23.810
on the street there.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.012
It turns out they were

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.947
others were taken to area hospitals.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.082
They've had to open up

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.884
extra hospital beds.

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.485
You have the president of South Korea.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.687
He convened an emergency meeting of

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:37.524
of his of his disaster management team.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:37.857
They have it

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.559
they have a disaster management

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.694
medical team on scene here now.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.363
So this is a federal

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.532
this is a federal incident.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.301
Undoubtedly got to be one of the worst

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.135
that they've seen here

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.403
in Seoul in quite some time,

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.037
although I don't have

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.038
historical statistics

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:52.772
to back that up yet.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.740
But just

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.242
the looks on people's faces out here

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.644
looks of disbelief

00:02:57.644 --> 00:03:01.247
at these scenes of of hundreds

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:01.981
and hundreds

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.150
of of emergency medical personnel

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:08.388
and earlier just rows of people's

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.390
bodies on the street.

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:14.561
So whether some sort of

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:15.695
media area here, Fred.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.462
Yeah, go ahead. Yes.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.096
So I'm wondering, John,

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.498
I just want to make sure I understand.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.332
So you're saying

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.667
the party was taking place

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.869
inside the hotel.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:23.803
Something happened

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.171
and then there was a stampede

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.040
and it was outside in

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.475
which people would just start collapsing

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.378
or were there people

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.080
who who

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.081
were physically in trouble

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.584
and had been taken out of the building?

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.952
And then you saw,

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:39.752
you know,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.254
what appeared to be bodies

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.556
on the ground with sheets over

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.460
So that's a very good question.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.062
One thing I'll point out to you

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.396
is that if you look at

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.465
if we can actually give you a wide look,

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.300
if you look at the sidewalks around

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.268
here, Charlie just said,

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.337
you know, it's not it's not a very, very

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.539
narrow area here.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.341
And this is an area where earlier

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.476
there were videos of people on the ground

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.645
So while we're still trying

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:07.947
to piece together from authorities

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.883
exactly how this all went down,

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:11.618
what is clear

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.152
is that there were a lot of people

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.488
crowded into a particular area

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:16.723
and at least 81

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.490
people called

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.524
saying that they couldn't breathe.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.926
They called emergency services

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.628
saying that they had trouble breathing.

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:24.063
You had cardiac arrest you know.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.332
59 people dying.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.301
Were people who fell?

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:30.036
Were they crushed

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.070
where most of the deaths

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:31.904
from cardiac arrest?

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.206
We're still waiting for the specifics.

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:33.840
Fred.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.375
Clearly, there are a lot of questions

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.076
that still need to be answered here.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.177
This is an investigation

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.846
that is just getting underway

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.981
and they have so much work to do.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.116
Not to mention

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.651
notifying the families of those

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:45.652
are really going

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:46.986
to make it home for this Halloween party.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.454
Oh, it's heartbreaking.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.956
Will Ripley, thank you so much.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.624
So, of course,

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.892
still trying to figure out what

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.327
what may have induced

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:57.697
cardiac arrest or suffocation,

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:01.100
what led to the deaths of now.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.069
59 people there and

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.504
so many others injured.

